1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,800
Hello again!

2
00:00:01,220 --> 00:00:05,120
Last time, we learned big friend adding.

3
00:00:05,780 --> 00:00:07,040
Do you remember the trick?

4
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:12,160
Take away the friend, then carry to the tens rod.

5
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:16,740
This video is all about big friend taking away.

6
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:18,960
Same friends.

7
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:20,420
Same idea.

8
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:22,140
Just the other way round.

9
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:23,380
Ready?

10
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:24,500
Let us go!

11
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:28,680
First, always look at the ones rod.

12
00:00:29,580 --> 00:00:32,380
If there are enough beads, just take them away.

13
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:33,640
Watch.

14
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:36,420
Eighteen take away five.

15
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:38,600
Push the upper bead up.

16
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:39,520
Done!

17
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:41,000
Thirteen.

18
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:42,600
That was easy.

19
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:44,640
The ones rod had enough.

20
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:48,620
Now let us try ten take away one.

21
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:50,540
Make ten.

22
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:54,860
One bead on the tens rod, and nothing on the ones rod.

23
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:57,280
Look at the ones rod.

24
00:00:57,980 --> 00:00:59,820
How many beads can we take away?

25
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:01,600
None!

26
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:03,960
The ones rod is empty.

27
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:05,640
Oh no.

28
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:07,120
We are stuck.

29
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:09,160
Do not worry.

30
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:11,280
A big friend can help us.

31
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:13,920
We want to take away one.

32
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,220
Who is one's friend?

33
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:18,100
Nine!

34
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:20,880
One and nine make ten.

35
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:24,900
So here is the big friend trick for taking away.

36
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:31,400
Take away one is the same as add nine, then take away ten.

37
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:36,340
Minus one equals plus nine, minus ten.

38
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:38,440
Why does it work?

39
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:42,380
Taking away ten takes away too much.

40
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:44,640
It takes away nine extra.

41
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:48,000
So we add the nine back first.

42
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,120
And we are left with taking away one.

43
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:54,220
Let us do it on the abacus.

44
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:56,720
Remember our rule.

45
00:01:57,640 --> 00:02:02,780
The ones rod goes first, and lower beads move before the upper bead.

46
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:06,600
First, add nine on the ones rod.

47
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:11,320
Push four lower beads up, then the upper bead down.

48
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:14,680
Now the tens rod gets its turn.

49
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:16,740
Take away ten.

50
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:20,100
Take one bead away from the tens rod.

51
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:22,560
And there it is.

52
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:23,340
Nine!

53
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:26,500
Ten take away one is nine.

54
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:29,400
Plus nine, minus ten.

55
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:33,980
That is our first big friend formula for taking away.

56
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:37,640
Let us try twelve take away three.

57
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:39,440
Make twelve.

58
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:44,800
One bead on the tens rod, and two lower beads on the ones rod.

59
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:48,620
Can we take away three from the ones rod?

60
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:50,180
No!

61
00:02:50,540 --> 00:02:52,440
There are only two beads there.

62
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:55,320
So we call a big friend.

63
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:58,120
Three's friend is seven.

64
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:03,420
Minus three equals plus seven, minus ten.

65
00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:05,900
Ones rod first.

66
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:07,520
Add seven.

67
00:03:08,340 --> 00:03:12,160
Push two lower beads up, then the upper bead down.

68
00:03:13,540 --> 00:03:16,380
Now take one bead away from the tens rod.

69
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:19,920
Twelve take away three is nine!

70
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:22,780
You are doing so well!

71
00:03:23,340 --> 00:03:26,420
Give this video a like, and subscribe for more.

72
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:31,640
Now, what about taking away a big number, like seven?

73
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:35,520
Let us try eleven take away seven.

74
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:37,360
Make eleven.

75
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:42,740
One bead on the tens rod, and one lower bead on the ones rod.

76
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:46,960
Can we take away seven from just one bead?

77
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:48,960
No way!

78
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:51,440
Seven's friend is three.

79
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:56,740
Minus seven equals plus three, minus ten.

80
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,080
Ones rod first.

81
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:01,600
Push three lower beads up.

82
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:05,680
Then take one bead away from the tens rod.

83
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:09,160
Eleven take away seven is four!

84
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:12,620
The big numbers work the same way.

85
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,880
Now stop and look.

86
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:16,780
Did you see it?

87
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:21,500
Every single time, we did the same two things.

88
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:24,840
Add the friend on the ones rod first.

89
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,900
Then take one bead away from the tens rod.

90
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:30,900
The friend changes.

91
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:32,980
But ten never does.

92
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:39,360
There is one for every number, from take away one to take away nine.

93
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:43,840
That is nine big friend formulas for taking away.

94
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,260
Now it is your turn.

95
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:47,800
All on your own.

96
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:49,560
Make thirteen.

97
00:04:50,660 --> 00:04:55,340
One bead on the tens rod, and three lower beads on the ones rod.

98
00:04:56,780 --> 00:04:57,900
Take away nine.

99
00:04:59,040 --> 00:04:59,440
Think.

100
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:01,460
What is nine's friend?

101
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:03,960
One!

102
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:08,260
Minus nine equals plus one, minus ten.

103
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:15,400
Add one lower bead on the ones rod, then take one bead away from the tens rod.

104
00:05:16,620 --> 00:05:18,460
What number is showing now?

105
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:22,280
Thirteen take away nine is four!

106
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:23,900
Did you get it?

107
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:25,120
Well done!

108
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:29,120
So now you know big friend taking away.

109
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:32,520
Nine formulas, and they are all yours.

110
00:05:33,260 --> 00:05:36,280
Try them at home on your own abacus.

111
00:05:36,740 --> 00:05:41,160
Search for Abacus Kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

112
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:43,040
Download it free.

113
00:05:43,860 --> 00:05:48,760
Next time, we will mix everything together in one big game.

114
00:05:49,660 --> 00:05:50,800
See you next time!
